Oh, sure it is. Before there were cats, my dogs included Lunch, Meal on
the Hoof, Meatball Sub, Pronto Pup, Corndog, Famine, Gulper, Gnasher,
Touch it You're Dead, Tooth Gritter, Tooth Gnasher (after Thor's cart
goats), Chow Hound, Moving Mouth, Fetch, Bat Snapper, Underfoot, Spot,
Muttley, and others too numerous to mention in a mixed crowd. On a
shared system with bones files, something either obscene or scatological
is always in order. You really don't want somebody finding your ghost
guarded by a dog named Dog, do you? Pretty soon your friends will be
looking at you out of eye corners and you'll stop getting party
invitations.

When cats were added, I didn't need much imagination; I just used my
house cats' names: Pickpocket, Amber, Vanilla, Jonquil, and Treacle. So
far, that's always been enough.

>What you ought to ask for is fruit names.  I'm rather fond of pieces of
>fibreglass insulation, myself.  8-P  Mmm.  

Tough as heck to juice those, though.

Cold pizza, guano, hester lye soda, and fewmeets have always been old
favorites.  Aqua regia is a nice touch.  Papaya, mango, kiwi (my current
choice), MK41 grenade, and bite block are other popular choices.

